    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all 3 tests pass with a `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional owner `email` field end-to-end so it satisfies the specification (valid when present, stored/returned lower-cased, `400` when present-but-invalid), and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `email` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (`type: string, format: email, maxLength: 255`). Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields`, this puts `email` on both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`), and generates a `@Email` bean-validation annotation enforced via the existing `@Valid` request binding.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added an `email` column (`@Column(name = \"email\")`, `@Email`) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it by name, so no mapper change was needed.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `normalizeEmail(...)` helper (with an `EMAIL_PATTERN` constant) called from both `addOwner` and `updateOwner`. When email is present it validates syntax (rejecting invalid input with `400` via the existing `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` path) and writes it back trimmed and lower-cased so it is stored/returned lower-cased; absent/blank email is left untouched (optional).\n\n4. **Schema SQL** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`) \u2014 Added the `email` column to the `owners` table (tests use `ddl-auto=none` + `schema.sql`).\n\n5. **Seed data** (`db/hsqldb/data.sql`, `db/mysql/data.sql`) \u2014 The column-less `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)` statements broke once a column was added, so I gave them explicit column lists (email defaults to NULL). The h2/postgres seed files already used explicit column lists.\n\nValidation is enforced at two layers (the generated `@Email` at request binding and the controller's explicit check), both returning `400`; the test log confirms the invalid `not-an-email` case is rejected and `Test.User@Example.COM` is persisted and read back as `test.user@example.com`.",
